# Plural cases in Russian: дети, детей, детьми
subtitle: "Tea and a family photo with Нина Петровна: the Russian plural in all six cases in one table, and the family words that break it: дети, люди, сыновья, дочери."
tags: ["russian","russian plural cases","дети","russian family","russian grammar"]
teaches: ["grammar/plural-cases","grammar/case-tables","vocabulary/family"]
thumb: "band \"The plural is easier. Mostly.\""
voices: {"a":"gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would","b":"gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated"}
next: {"title":"Asking whether in Russian: ли","href":"https://www.drawcast.app/#gh=hmelberg/drawcast-library/russian-from-zero/113-russian-whether.cast"}

