      ms: 2480
      voice: gemini:Leda | a friendly young Russian woman from Moscow, natural and lively, speaks English with a light Russian accent and says Russian words natively; never exaggerated
    '|a||Where does her son (сын) live?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3000
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Сын живёт в Москве́: in Moscow.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3480
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Where does her daughter (дочь) live?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3120
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||А дочь — здесь, в Петербу́рге: here, in Petersburg.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4520
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||How many grandchildren (вну́ки) does she have?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3680
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Три вну́ка и одна́ вну́чка: three grandsons and a granddaughter, four in all.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6760
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Today: the plural in all six cases, starting with her photo. Ни́на Петро́вна is the ба́бушка.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8080
      voice: gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would
    '|a||Сын и его́ жена́, his wife, живу́т в Москве́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:13nxr'
    '|a||Дочь и её муж, her husband, живу́т здесь.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:n0hgd5'
    '|a||У сы́на одна́ дочь: вну́чка, a granddaughter.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:ahotmy'
    '|a||У до́чери три сы́на: вну́ки, grandsons.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1bfin76'
    '|a||One child is ребёнок; many are де́ти, a different word.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5960
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1bslha7'
    '|a||Челове́к, a person; many are лю́ди, which you met in lesson 52.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:mt94nt'
    '|a||Сын, сыновья́.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:i8brcb'
    '|a||Друг, друзья́: both plurals grow -ья.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:3wmu9h'
    '|a||And дочь, до́чери, daughters, with an extra -ер-. У до́чери, of a daughter, looks the same.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1twd6kg'
    '|a||At home, Ни́на Петро́вна says до́чка.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:8k4d4r'
    '|a||Now one regular word, внук, in all six cases: one on the left, many on the right.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:yrt6vc'
    '|a||Мой внук, мои́ вну́ки.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:84sl9l'
    '|a||Кому́? Мои́м вну́кам.':
