      ms: 2520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1kdf8eh'
    '|a||С кем? С мои́ми вну́ками.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:32qpeg'
    '|a||О ком? О мои́х вну́ках.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 2640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:zc92vs'
    '|a||-ам, -ами, -ах, or -ям, -ями, -ях after a soft stem: almost every noun, he, she or it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:c33ml7'
    '|a||Ви́жу мои́х вну́ков. Нет мои́х вну́ков.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:17fwmf8'
    '|a||For people and animals, the object copies the of-plural; for things, the plain row. So the of-row is the one to learn: -ов, -ей, or no ending at all.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1pd70zl'
    '|a||And мой has only four plural forms: мои́, мои́х, мои́м, мои́ми.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:93qrci'
    '|a||Adjectives go the same way: мои́ ста́рые друзья́, my old friends in London.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:u0fkwc'
    '|a||Я ча́сто ду́маю о мои́х ста́рых друзья́х.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 3400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1ygkwzn'
    '|a||Ста́рые, ста́рых, ста́рым, ста́рыми: four endings, every gender.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | Tom, a warm, easy-going English speaker who knows Russian well; friendly with Masha, clear and unhurried; says Russian words the way a native Russian speaker would #ctx:1pomul2'
    '|a||Now the two odd words.':
